        "question": "How is the update gate implemented in a GRU?",
        "depth": "normal",
        "work_id": "AI-CSE-III-I-GRU-NOTES",
        "answer": "The update gate \\( z_t \\) decides how much of the previous hidden state (\\( h_{t-1} \\)) should be retained for the next time step. It operates using the equation:\n\n\\[ r_t = \\sigma(W_r \\cdot [h_{t}, x_t] + b_r) \\]\n\nHere, \\( W_r \\) represents weight matrix, \\( b_r \\)'s are biases, and \\( \\sigma \\) is the sigmoid function. This gate multiplies the previous state by its output to determine what parts of the old state to retain.",
